I saw this advice very often in the newsgroup. But I don't agree at
all. My current character is rather simple (Archeologist, with
Str:25,Dex:15) and has killed on his way down in Gehennom about 10
Master Liches. They aren't that strong if you have some good equipment
AND a good strategy to kill them:

the equipment:
- you need magic resistance (GDSM works best because it gives you "mucho"
  AC and you don't have to worry about its weight)
- you need a good weapon (i have the +6 grayswandir; oh i love it!)
- you have to be very fast (speed boots will do or a potion of speed in time)
- may be you should be very lucky as this character is (I think it
  helps you resisting the magic attacks of the Master Lich, but I'm
  not sure at all)

the strategy:
- you have to be unburdend!!! (since the lich usually summons dragons or
  read scrolls to create them)
- locate them with your telepathy if you go down into a new level
- wait on the up staircase!! (because they regenerate there)
- they will teleport some turns later right next to you and attack
- keep standing on the staircase and *hack* them

I know this equipment is hard to get but its really(!) challenging
not to genocide at all and to fight.

To be true, this character hasn't found a scroll of genocide, that's why
I had to develop this conduct. But it works great, yeah!

